prompts.user_request:
Your task is to rewrite the provided academic discussion transcript into a self-contained, formal, and meticulous .tex latex document, closely following these guidelines:
<guidelines>
1. The rewrite should meticulously reflect all information from the discussion, maintaining the logical flow of ideas.
2. Ensure that every concept and equation mentioned in the transcription is included and elaborated upon.
3. Use appropriate LaTeX commands to typeset mathematical equations and expressions.
4. Use  \begin{align} and \end{align} for dispalyed multi-line equations. The note should be highly mathematical and technical. Use as many equations as possible.
5. Convert the conversational style of the transcript into formal, precise, and technical language appropriate.
6. If visual inputs are provided (such as images of the whiteboard), include them coherently in the LaTeX document. Use the images to help scribing equations and figures.
7. I repeat, the output document should be faithful to the original discussion. IT IS NOT A SUMMARY. IT IS A METICULOUS REWRITE OF THE ORIGINAL DISCUSSION INTO A FORMAL LATEX DOCUMENT.
</guidelines>

Organize the LaTeX document using this template:
<latex_template>
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb,amsthm}

\title{[Insert appropriate title]}
\author{Based on a discussion between [list participants]}
\date{[Insert date of discussion]}

\begin{document}

\maketitle

[Directly go into the discussion content]

Then we obtain...
\begin{align}
    % the equation
\end{align}
where $X$ is the variable and $Y$ is the variable. [use the align environment without line breaks]

[Insert content here]

[more to cover all the topics in the discussion]

\bibliographystyle{plain}
\bibliography{library}

\end{document}
</latex_template>

Output the LaTeX document inside the <latex_document></latex_document> tags.
